 }\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_code\":\"import java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.List;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static double[] distances(double centerX, double centerY, String[] nuclei) {\\n        List<Double> result = new ArrayList<>();\\n        for (String nucleus : nuclei) {\\n            double[] point = parsePoint(nucleus);\\n            if (point == null) {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            result.add(Math.hypot(point[0] - centerX, point[1] - centerY));\\n        }\\n\\n        double[] distances = new double[result.size()];\\n        for (int i = 0; i < result.size(); i++) {\\n            distances[i] = result.get(i);\\n        }\\n        return distances;\\n    }\\n\\n    private static double[] parsePoint(String text) {\\n        if (text == null) {\\n            return null;\\n        }\\n        String[] fields = text.split(\\\",\\\", -1);\\n        if (fields.length != 2 || fields[0].trim().isEmpty() || fields[1].trim().isEmpty()) {\\n            return null;\\n        }\\n        try {\\n            double x = Double.parseDouble(fields[0].trim());\\n            double y = Double.parseDouble(fields[1].trim());\\n            if (!Double.isFinite(x) || !Double.isFinite(y)) {\\n                return null;\\n            }\\n            return new double[] {x, y};\\n        } catch (NumberFormatException exception) {\\n            return null;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_label\":\"Stops scanning at the first malformed coordinate instead of skipping it and processing later valid elements.\"},{\"id\":\"cap-v2-sequence_algorithms-java-repair-02\",\"problem\":\"Repair the program below. Implement `public static byte[] mergeSegments(byte[][] segments)` in a public final class `Solution`.\\n\\n`segments` is a non-null ordered array of binary manuscript segments. A null inner array is a malformed segment and must be ignored. Concatenate every non-null segment in input order, preserving every byte, including bytes from empty or repeated segments. Return a newly allocated array; changes subsequently made to any input segment must not affect the result.\\n\\nReturn a corrected complete `Solution.java`. Use only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.\\n\\nKnown-bad source:\\n```java\\nimport java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static byte[] mergeSegments(byte[][] segments) {\\n        ByteArrayOutputStream merged = new ByteArrayOutputStream();\\n        for (byte[] segment : segments) {\\n            if (segment == null) {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            merged.write(segment, 0, segment.length);\\n        }\\n        return merged.toByteArray();\\n    }\\n}\\n```\",\"reference_code\":\"import java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static byte[] mergeSegments(byte[][] segments) {\\n        ByteArrayOutputStream merged = new ByteArrayOutputStream();\\n        for (byte[] segment : segments) {\\n            if (segment == null) {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            merged.write(segment, 0, segment.length);\\n        }\\n        return merged.toByteArray();\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_code\":\"import java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static byte[] mergeSegments(byte[][] segments) {\\n        ByteArrayOutputStream merged = new ByteArrayOutputStream();\\n        for (byte[] segment : segments) {\\n            if (segment == null) {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            merged.write(segment, 0, segment.length);\\n        }\\n        return merged.toByteArray();\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_label\":\"Treats a malformed null segment as the end of the sequence, dropping all valid segments that follow it.\"},{\"id\":\"cap-v2-stateful_workflows-java-generation-01\",\"problem\":\"Create a complete `Solution.java` containing a public final class `Solution` and the method `public static String[] manage(String[] commands)`.\\n\\nThe method manages an in-memory collection of jobs. Each job has one of four states: `CREATED`, `RUNNING`, `DONE`, or `CANCELLED`. Commands are processed sequentially and are guaranteed to use one of these syntactically valid forms:\\n\\n- `CREATE id`: create a new job in `CREATED`. Each created identifier is unique.\\n- `START id`: change `CREATED` to `RUNNING`.\\n- `COMPLETE id`: change `RUNNING` to `DONE`.\\n- `CANCEL id`: change `CREATED` or `RUNNING` to `CANCELLED`.\\n- `LIST`: report all jobs.\\n\\nEvery non-`CREATE` job command refers to an existing job. If its transition is not allowed from the job's current state, leave that state unchanged. For each job command, append one output string in the form `id=STATE`, reflecting the state after processing it. For each `LIST`, append one string containing all jobs as `id=STATE` entries separated by semicolons. A `LIST` must always use job creation order, regardless of later transitions. If no jobs exist, its output is the empty string. Return all output strings in command order.\\n\\nUse only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.\",\"reference_code\":\"import java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.LinkedHashMap;\\nimport java.util.List;\\nimport java.util.Map;\\nimport java.util.StringJoiner;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    private enum State {\\n        CREATED, RUNNING, DONE, CANCELLED\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] manage(String[] commands) {\\n        Map<String, State> jobs = new LinkedHashMap<>();\\n        List<String> output = new ArrayList<>();\\n\\n        for (String command : commands) {\\n            if (command.equals(\\\"LIST\\\")) {\\n                StringJoiner listing = new StringJoiner(\\\";\\\");\\n                for (Map.Entry<String, State> entry : jobs.entrySet()) {\\n                    listing.add(entry.getKey() + \\\"=\\\" + entry.getValue());\\n                }\\n                output.add(listing.toString());\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n\\n            int separator = command.indexOf(' ');\\n            String action = command.substring(0, separator);\\n            String id = command.substring(separator + 1);\\n\\n            if (action.equals(\\\"CREATE\\\")) {\\n                jobs.put(id, State.CREATED);\\n            } else {\\n                State state = jobs.get(id);\\n                if (action.equals(\\\"START\\\") && state == State.CREATED) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.RUNNING);\\n                } else if (action.equals(\\\"COMPLETE\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.DONE);\\n                } else if (action.equals(\\\"CANCEL\\\")\\n                        && (state == State.CREATED || state == State.RUNNING)) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.CANCELLED);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            output.add(id + \\\"=\\\" + jobs.get(id));\\n        }\\n\\n        return output.toArray(new String[0]);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_code\":\"import java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.HashMap;\\nimport java.util.List;\\nimport java.util.Map;\\nimport java.util.StringJoiner;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    private enum State {\\n        CREATED, RUNNING, DONE, CANCELLED\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] manage(String[] commands) {\\n        Map<String, State> jobs = new HashMap<>();\\n        List<String> output = new ArrayList<>();\\n\\n        for (String command : commands) {\\n            if (command.equals(\\\"LIST\\\")) {\\n                StringJoiner listing = new StringJoiner(\\\";\\\");\\n                for (Map.Entry<String, State> entry : jobs.entrySet()) {\\n                    listing.add(entry.getKey() + \\\"=\\\" + entry.getValue());\\n                }\\n                output.add(listing.toString());\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n\\n            int separator = command.indexOf(' ');\\n            String action = command.substring(0, separator);\\n            String id = command.substring(separator + 1);\\n\\n            if (action.equals(\\\"CREATE\\\")) {\\n                jobs.put(id, State.CREATED);\\n            } else {\\n                State state = jobs.get(id);\\n                if (action.equals(\\\"START\\\") && state == State.CREATED) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.RUNNING);\\n                } else if (action.equals(\\\"COMPLETE\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.DONE);\\n                } else if (action.equals(\\\"CANCEL\\\")\\n                        && (state == State.CREATED || state == State.RUNNING)) {\\n                    jobs.put(id, State.CANCELLED);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            output.add(id + \\\"=\\\" + jobs.get(id));\\n        }\\n\\n        return output.toArray(new String[0]);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_label\":\"Stores jobs in a HashMap, so LIST output does not guarantee the required stable creation order.\"},{\"id\":\"cap-v2-stateful_workflows-java-generation-02\",\"problem\":\"Create a complete `Solution.java` containing a public final class `Solution` and the method `public static String[] transact(int initialBalance, String[] commands)`.\\n\\nProcess the commands as a single-account transaction workflow. At most one transaction can be active. Commands are syntactically valid and use these forms:\\n\\n- `BEGIN id`: if no transaction is active, begin transaction `id` with a pending adjustment of zero and output `BEGIN id`; otherwise output `ERROR` without changing anything. Identifiers of successfully begun transactions are unique.\\n- `ADD amount`: if a transaction is active, add the signed integer amount to its pending adjustment and output `PENDING n`, where `n` is the new pending adjustment; otherwise output `ERROR`.\\n- `COMMIT`: if active, add the pending adjustment to the account balance, append an audit entry `id=balance`, end the transaction, and output `COMMIT id balance`; otherwise output `ERROR`.\\n- `ROLLBACK`: if active, discard its pending adjustment, end the transaction, and output `ROLLBACK id balance`, where `balance` is the unchanged account balance; otherwise output `ERROR`.\\n- `HISTORY`: output all committed audit entries separated by semicolons, or the empty string if none exist.\\n\\nAll parsed amounts, pending adjustments, and balances fit in `int`. Audit entries returned by every `HISTORY` command must remain in commit order, even when transaction identifiers have a different lexical order. Return one output string for each input command, in command order.\\n\\nUse only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.\",\"reference_code\":\"import java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.List;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] transact(int initialBalance, String[] commands) {\\n        int balance = initialBalance;\\n        String activeId = null;\\n        int pending = 0;\\n        List<String> history = new ArrayList<>();\\n        List<String> output = new ArrayList<>();\\n\\n        for (String command : commands) {\\n            if (command.startsWith(\\\"BEGIN \\\")) {\\n                if (activeId != null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    activeId = command.substring(6);\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                    output.add(\\\"BEGIN \\\" + activeId);\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.startsWith(\\\"ADD \\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    pending += Integer.parseInt(command.substring(4));\\n                    output.add(\\\"PENDING \\\" + pending);\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.equals(\\\"COMMIT\\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    balance += pending;\\n                    history.add(activeId + \\\"=\\\" + balance);\\n                    output.add(\\\"COMMIT \\\" + activeId + \\\" \\\" + balance);\\n                    activeId = null;\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.equals(\\\"ROLLBACK\\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ROLLBACK \\\" + activeId + \\\" \\\" + balance);\\n                    activeId = null;\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                output.add(String.join(\\\";\\\", history));\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        return output.toArray(new String[0]);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_code\":\"import java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.Collections;\\nimport java.util.List;\\n\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] transact(int initialBalance, String[] commands) {\\n        int balance = initialBalance;\\n        String activeId = null;\\n        int pending = 0;\\n        List<String> history = new ArrayList<>();\\n        List<String> output = new ArrayList<>();\\n\\n        for (String command : commands) {\\n            if (command.startsWith(\\\"BEGIN \\\")) {\\n                if (activeId != null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    activeId = command.substring(6);\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                    output.add(\\\"BEGIN \\\" + activeId);\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.startsWith(\\\"ADD \\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    pending += Integer.parseInt(command.substring(4));\\n                    output.add(\\\"PENDING \\\" + pending);\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.equals(\\\"COMMIT\\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    balance += pending;\\n                    history.add(activeId + \\\"=\\\" + balance);\\n                    output.add(\\\"COMMIT \\\" + activeId + \\\" \\\" + balance);\\n                    activeId = null;\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                }\\n            } else if (command.equals(\\\"ROLLBACK\\\")) {\\n                if (activeId == null) {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ERROR\\\");\\n                } else {\\n                    output.add(\\\"ROLLBACK \\\" + activeId + \\\" \\\" + balance);\\n                    activeId = null;\\n                    pending = 0;\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                List<String> sorted = new ArrayList<>(history);\\n                Collections.sort(sorted);\\n                output.add(String.join(\\\";\\\", sorted));\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        return output.toArray(new String[0]);\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_label\":\"Sorts audit entries lexically for HISTORY instead of preserving their stable commit order.\"},{\"id\":\"cap-v2-stateful_workflows-java-repair-01\",\"problem\":\"Repair the program below. Implement `public static String[] finalStates(String[][] workflows)` in a public final class `Solution`.\\n\\nEach inner array describes a separate workflow and contains only the commands `START`, `PAUSE`, `RESUME`, and `FINISH`. Every workflow must begin independently in state `NEW`. Process its commands in order using these transitions:\\n\\n- `START`: `NEW` to `RUNNING`\\n- `PAUSE`: `RUNNING` to `PAUSED`\\n- `RESUME`: `PAUSED` to `RUNNING`\\n- `FINISH`: `RUNNING` to `DONE`\\n\\nA command without a transition from the current state leaves the state unchanged. Return one state name per workflow in outer-array order. State from one workflow must never affect another workflow. Both array levels are non-null.\\n\\nReturn a corrected complete `Solution.java`. Use only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.\\n\\nKnown-bad source:\\n```java\\npublic final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    private enum State {\\n        NEW, RUNNING, PAUSED, DONE\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] finalStates(String[][] workflows) {\\n        String[] result = new String[workflows.length];\\n        State state = State.NEW;\\n\\n        for (int i = 0; i < workflows.length; i++) {\\n            for (String command : workflows[i]) {\\n                if (command.equals(\\\"START\\\") && state == State.NEW) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"PAUSE\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.PAUSED;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"RESUME\\\") && state == State.PAUSED) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"FINISH\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.DONE;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            result[i] = state.name();\\n        }\\n        return result;\\n    }\\n}\\n```\",\"reference_code\":\"public final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    private enum State {\\n        NEW, RUNNING, PAUSED, DONE\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] finalStates(String[][] workflows) {\\n        String[] result = new String[workflows.length];\\n\\n        for (int i = 0; i < workflows.length; i++) {\\n            State state = State.NEW;\\n            for (String command : workflows[i]) {\\n                if (command.equals(\\\"START\\\") && state == State.NEW) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"PAUSE\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.PAUSED;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"RESUME\\\") && state == State.PAUSED) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"FINISH\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.DONE;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            result[i] = state.name();\\n        }\\n        return result;\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_code\":\"public final class Solution {\\n    private Solution() {\\n    }\\n\\n    private enum State {\\n        NEW, RUNNING, PAUSED, DONE\\n    }\\n\\n    public static String[] finalStates(String[][] workflows) {\\n        String[] result = new String[workflows.length];\\n        State state = State.NEW;\\n\\n        for (int i = 0; i < workflows.length; i++) {\\n            for (String command : workflows[i]) {\\n                if (command.equals(\\\"START\\\") && state == State.NEW) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"PAUSE\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.PAUSED;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"RESUME\\\") && state == State.PAUSED) {\\n                    state = State.RUNNING;\\n                } else if (command.equals(\\\"FINISH\\\") && state == State.RUNNING) {\\n                    state = State.DONE;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            result[i] = state.name();\\n        }\\n        return result;\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"known_bad_label\":\"Initializes the workflow state only once, allowing the final state of one workflow to leak into the next.\"}]}"}}
