Each element of `nuclei` is intended to contain two decimal coordinates separated by exactly one comma, such as `"12.5, 7"`. An element is malformed if it is null, does not contain exactly two fields, has a blank field, contains a value that cannot be parsed as a `double`, or contains a non-finite value. Skip malformed elements. For every valid element, calculate its Euclidean distance from `(centerX, centerY)` using `Math.hypot`. Return the distances in the same relative order as their valid source elements. `nuclei` is non-null, and the center coordinates are finite.

Return a corrected complete `Solution.java`. Use only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.

